      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your sister's exhaustion and obligation to help you can be misinterpreted as genuine support, but it can also be rooted in a sense of duty and obligation, rather than genuine concern for your well-being. Letting go of proximity and support doesn't necessarily mean you're abandoning your sister; it might mean giving her the space to rediscover her own life, interests, and desires. By removing yourself from the dynamic, you can create space for your sister to find her own path and rediscover her sense of purpose and fulfillment.",
